1252
01:38:36,156 --> 01:38:37,617
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes it gets lost.

1253
01:38:37,977 --> 01:38:43,200
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes... it happens even for Arya.

1254
01:38:43,260 --> 01:38:46,682
[SPEAKER_00]: It is just because of Buddha generally.

1255
01:38:51,445 --> 01:39:04,072
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, look... For Arya, less and less, and... for an Arahant, forgetting things, like forgetting particular things,

1256
01:39:05,316 --> 01:39:07,557
[SPEAKER_02]: does not induce ignorance anymore.

1257
01:39:09,339 --> 01:39:12,381
[SPEAKER_02]: So, when you forget something, then you remember it.

1258
01:39:13,001 --> 01:39:15,643
[SPEAKER_02]: There was no ignorance induced in you forgetting.

1259
01:39:17,544 --> 01:39:22,047
[SPEAKER_02]: No sense of self induced, no appropriation induced, no upādāna induced.

1260
01:39:23,228 --> 01:39:25,049
[SPEAKER_02]: For Putujana, that's not the case.

1261
01:39:26,170 --> 01:39:28,912
[SPEAKER_02]: When Putujana forgets, his habits

1262
01:39:30,041 --> 01:39:37,144
[SPEAKER_02]: When he's in the state of forgetfulness, our habits of contusion, our habits that maintain avidya and everything else.

1263
01:39:39,505 --> 01:39:45,447
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's why, like, you cannot possibly be a hundred percent mindful all the time.

1264
01:39:45,507 --> 01:39:46,468
[SPEAKER_02]: It doesn't work like that.

1265
01:39:48,368 --> 01:39:53,811
[SPEAKER_02]: But what you want to do is to try and be mindful as much as you can, and while you're mindful, understand the things.

1266
01:39:53,911 --> 01:39:55,972
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, when you forget, like, when...

1267
01:39:59,046 --> 01:40:10,974
[SPEAKER_02]: When Arahant's bodhisattvas, when they were... Well, when, like, Uvayda Rādhā was still a sotāpanna, and when Sariputta died, he was very shaken, he was very affected by it.

1268
01:40:11,134 --> 01:40:19,800
[SPEAKER_02]: He said, everything went black, and the clouds were dark, and I couldn't... Twenty years I've been serving the Lord and listening to dhamma, and I couldn't remember a single thing.

1269
01:40:21,081 --> 01:40:22,942
[SPEAKER_02]: But that doesn't mean that he stopped being a sotāpanna.

1270
01:40:23,242 --> 01:40:27,245
[SPEAKER_02]: It means when, whatever the pressing circumstances were gone,

1271
01:40:29,168 --> 01:40:31,629
[SPEAKER_02]: Things were back to normal often earlier.

1272
01:40:32,109 --> 01:40:38,911
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes I feel, when really such mindfulness is lost, I actually wonder, what does this sense of self mean?

1273
01:40:38,971 --> 01:40:41,552
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes you can forget the body means what?

1274
01:40:41,572 --> 01:40:44,552
[SPEAKER_00]: Because body means, basically, I must... Yeah, well, no.

1275
01:40:44,572 --> 01:40:53,155
[SPEAKER_02]: Sense of self is, when you are reflecting, when you're thinking, whether mindfully or not, there is an implication of me.

1276
01:40:54,632 --> 01:40:55,552
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the sense of self.

1277
01:40:55,932 --> 01:40:56,673
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's what I meant.

1278
01:40:57,213 --> 01:41:09,056
[SPEAKER_02]: For an arahant, when he's not... when he might be forgetful in regard to things, that doesn't imply sense of self at all anymore.

1279
01:41:09,477 --> 01:41:16,179
[SPEAKER_02]: Because self and the whole appropriation thing is not in the things.

1280
01:41:16,399 --> 01:41:20,280
[SPEAKER_02]: It's in your relationship with the things, which means there is always a degree of awareness in that.

1281
01:41:21,470 --> 01:41:25,112
[SPEAKER_02]: So, forgetfulness is in regard to particular things.

1282
01:41:26,332 --> 01:41:30,354
[SPEAKER_02]: But forgetfulness as an experience is something you can be mindful of.

1283
01:41:32,255 --> 01:41:36,877
[SPEAKER_02]: I... it's present and it's something you... you don't have to forget.

1284
01:41:38,277 --> 01:41:40,899
[SPEAKER_02]: And on that level is the level where the sense of self arises.

1285
01:41:42,099 --> 01:41:48,182
[SPEAKER_02]: So that's why, like, even when the act of forgetting does not induce ignorance of sense of self anymore,

1286
01:41:49,172 --> 01:41:53,714
[SPEAKER_02]: That's when, you know, the mindfulness is being developed, when you can afford to forget particular things.

1287
01:41:54,654 --> 01:42:03,978
[SPEAKER_02]: But, obviously, you forget less and less of, like, the nature of things and, generally, your memory works better if the mindfulness is developed, because that's how memory works.

1288
01:42:05,799 --> 01:42:17,203
[SPEAKER_02]: And, as I said, if you remember, if you're remembering that you're here in this cave, if you don't forget that, whatever you're doing, on account of you being in the cave,

1289
01:42:17,688 --> 01:42:19,308
[SPEAKER_02]: You can be mindful in regard to that.

1290
01:42:21,629 --> 01:42:23,009
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, you forget that you're in the cave.

1291
01:42:23,329 --> 01:42:24,509
[SPEAKER_02]: But the thing is, you're still in the cave.

1292
01:42:25,509 --> 01:42:29,350
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, you can remember that you're in the cave and you establish your mindfulness of your situation.

1293
01:42:30,530 --> 01:42:33,311
[SPEAKER_02]: But I don't mean that now you just have to keep thinking, I'm in the cave, I'm in the cave.

1294
01:42:33,351 --> 01:42:33,451
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

1295
01:42:33,471 --> 01:42:40,652
[SPEAKER_02]: The point of mindfulness is to recognize this relationship between peripheral and actual, between general and particular.

1296
01:42:41,332 --> 01:42:42,713
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you're mindful in the cave.

1297
01:42:44,233 --> 01:42:44,653
[SPEAKER_02]: That's it.

1298
01:42:46,537 --> 01:42:50,758
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, through that mindfulness, while you're in the cave, do things.

1299
01:42:52,818 --> 01:42:54,158
[SPEAKER_02]: Talk, sit, walk, whatever.

1300
01:42:54,298 --> 01:42:56,379
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, you will be doing, inevitably, something.

1301
01:42:57,279 --> 01:42:58,559
[SPEAKER_02]: Even if it's nothing, I'm just sitting.

1302
01:42:58,579 --> 01:43:01,180
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, that's something you're doing while you're in the cave.

1303
01:43:02,680 --> 01:43:03,560
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's mindfulness.

1304
01:43:04,540 --> 01:43:08,241
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's like... that's how they... how the memory works.

1305
01:43:08,301 --> 01:43:13,062
[SPEAKER_02]: And if you read the suttas, that's why they always... when they're like...

1306
01:43:19,030 --> 01:43:22,393
[SPEAKER_02]: On one occasion, the Lord was staying in this province.

1307
01:43:23,433 --> 01:43:27,597
[SPEAKER_02]: While He was staying on that occasion in this province, He visited this forest.

1308
01:43:28,387 --> 01:43:33,031
[SPEAKER_02]: While he was staying in that province, visited this forest, he was sitting under the root of tree.

1309
01:43:33,752 --> 01:43:40,097
[SPEAKER_02]: While he was in the province, in that forest, at the root of the tree, these people came to visit.

1310
01:43:40,918 --> 01:43:45,422
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it's situation within situation within situation within situation within situation.

1311
01:43:45,502 --> 01:43:46,382
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's infinite.

1312
01:43:46,402 --> 01:43:47,063
[SPEAKER_02]: There's none to it.

1313
01:43:47,083 --> 01:43:50,746
[SPEAKER_02]: You can go as particular as you can observe and as general as you can hold.

1314
01:43:51,347 --> 01:43:51,767
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

1315
01:43:53,473 --> 01:43:56,535
[SPEAKER_02]: The point is not to kind of find the beginning with the end of it.

1316
01:43:56,615 --> 01:44:01,738
[SPEAKER_02]: The point is to fully understand the relationship between more general and then more particular.

1317
01:44:02,338 --> 01:44:04,059
[SPEAKER_02]: Because that's how mindfulness is established.

1318
01:44:04,840 --> 01:44:11,163
[SPEAKER_02]: So you don't have to necessarily start, oh, I'm in this province, in this forest, under this tree.

1319
01:44:12,464 --> 01:44:14,025
[SPEAKER_02]: You can just start with the body posture.

1320
01:44:15,040 --> 01:44:16,141
[SPEAKER_02]: Because it will be implied.

1321
01:44:16,501 --> 01:44:25,665
[SPEAKER_02]: Or you can just say, while I'm under this tree, at the root of the tree, these people came to visit.

1322
01:44:26,105 --> 01:44:29,747
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm still seated at the root of this tree, we were talking about this.

1323
01:44:30,507 --> 01:44:35,370
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm seated at the root of the tree, and we were talking about this, they asked me this particular question.

1324
01:44:35,430 --> 01:44:38,731
[SPEAKER_02]: Within that question, I gave this particular answer.

1325
01:44:38,811 --> 01:44:40,292
[SPEAKER_02]: And you end up remembering the whole thing.

1326
01:44:42,275 --> 01:44:45,877
[SPEAKER_02]: As opposed to linearly trying to list and just hold everything in mind at the same time.

1327
01:44:45,937 --> 01:44:46,777
[SPEAKER_02]: It doesn't work like that.

1328
01:44:49,538 --> 01:45:01,883
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's how sometimes there's a... like the establishments of mind in the suttas, when they... they would have said, the monk goes off and lives in the forest, and then he observes.

1329
01:45:01,903 --> 01:45:11,527
[SPEAKER_02]: While in this forest, any perceptions, feelings, disturbances, based on the perceptions of the village, cannot arise.

1330
01:45:13,478 --> 01:45:15,300
[SPEAKER_02]: Because I'm in the forest.

1331
01:45:16,060 --> 01:45:17,722
[SPEAKER_02]: So then, he sets his mind like that.

1332
01:45:18,523 --> 01:45:21,906
[SPEAKER_02]: Establishes it upon the perceptions of the forest.

1333
01:45:23,187 --> 01:45:32,416
[SPEAKER_02]: So, in the morning, when he goes Pindapa to the village, he might see unsuitable sights, hear unsuitable things, things that will provoke lust, aversion, delusion.

1334
01:45:33,416 --> 01:45:37,941
[SPEAKER_02]: But because his mind is established upon perception of the forest, none of these things can

1335
01:45:40,472 --> 01:45:43,713
[SPEAKER_02]: And then he reflects further.

1336
01:45:43,753 --> 01:45:51,935
[SPEAKER_02]: He says, Because I'm established upon the more refined perception of the forest, perceptions of the village cannot disturb me.

1337
01:45:52,715 --> 01:45:56,035
[SPEAKER_02]: Any disturbance that arises will be on account of perceptions of the forest.

1338
01:45:56,996 --> 01:45:59,536
[SPEAKER_02]: Because that's where the mind is.

1339
01:45:59,556 --> 01:46:00,636
[SPEAKER_02]: Then he can go even further.

1340
01:46:01,037 --> 01:46:05,778
[SPEAKER_02]: He can establish his mind upon the perception of the earth, as general as it is.

1341
01:46:07,118 --> 01:46:07,858
[SPEAKER_02]: Element of earth.

1342
01:46:09,695 --> 01:46:16,980
[SPEAKER_02]: And now, not even perceptions of the particular forest can bother him anymore, let alone the village.

1343
01:46:20,763 --> 01:46:22,845
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's like the contemplation of the four elements.

1344
01:46:23,305 --> 01:46:24,086
[SPEAKER_02]: That's how it works.

1345
01:46:25,347 --> 01:46:26,267
[SPEAKER_02]: More general, more than...

1346
01:46:26,647 --> 01:46:30,110
[SPEAKER_02]: The most general is earth, water, fire and air.

1347
01:46:30,770 --> 01:46:32,252
[SPEAKER_02]: It doesn't get more general than that.

1348
01:46:32,992 --> 01:46:36,495
[SPEAKER_02]: Yet, as subtle as it is, the mind can get established.

1349
01:46:37,498 --> 01:46:40,919
[SPEAKER_02]: And the Buddha said, be like earth, or be like fire.

1350
01:46:41,199 --> 01:46:48,280
[SPEAKER_02]: When you contemplate the nature of the earth, you get established through that mindfulness of... of earth.

1351
01:46:48,840 --> 01:46:52,601
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't even say element of earth, because for lots of people it implies a view element.

1352
01:46:52,801 --> 01:46:53,641
[SPEAKER_02]: No, just say earth.

1353
01:46:54,602 --> 01:47:01,123
[SPEAKER_02]: Designation earth stands for solidity, stands for heart, stands for earth.

1354
01:47:03,003 --> 01:47:03,483
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's it.

1355
01:47:03,603 --> 01:47:04,244
[SPEAKER_00]: Very interesting.

1356
01:47:04,704 --> 01:47:08,145
[SPEAKER_02]: You establish the mind... And that's the meditation on casinos, the ten casinos.

1357
01:47:08,165 --> 01:47:09,006
[SPEAKER_02]: That's exactly that.

1358
01:47:10,086 --> 01:47:11,607
[SPEAKER_02]: Now, nothing to do with what people do.

1359
01:47:12,347 --> 01:47:14,628
[SPEAKER_02]: Stare at colored discs and stuff like that.

1360
01:47:15,668 --> 01:47:18,330
[SPEAKER_01]: They're just for serious misunderstanding.

1361
01:47:19,770 --> 01:47:28,554
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, the ultimate casino, the ultimate establishment, is the establishment upon the casino of consciousness.

1362
01:47:32,008 --> 01:47:41,312
[SPEAKER_02]: So, in the same sense that you were established upon the perceptions of the forest and established upon earth and so on, you can get established upon consciousness.

1363
01:47:43,033 --> 01:47:43,253
[SPEAKER_02]: Why?

1364
01:47:43,333 --> 01:47:56,740
[SPEAKER_02]: Because if you establish upon the nature of presence in regard to that which is present, then whatever is present cannot disturb you.

1365
01:47:58,498 --> 01:48:03,542
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you're established in regard to the nature of presence of that which is present.

1366
01:48:04,183 --> 01:48:05,244
[SPEAKER_02]: So, it cannot disturb you.

1367
01:48:06,785 --> 01:48:12,390
[SPEAKER_02]: And, literally, whatever you experience is what is present, which means whatever you experience cannot disturb you.

1368
01:48:13,051 --> 01:48:17,254
[SPEAKER_02]: And the Buddha said that's the ultimate, that's the supreme, the most refined casino you can get established.

1369
01:48:17,915 --> 01:48:19,156
[SPEAKER_02]: But you don't need to go that far.

1370
01:48:19,256 --> 01:48:25,762
[SPEAKER_02]: Even the first element of earth is enough to abandon everything inferior to it, as the Buddha was referred to, which is evident.

1371
01:48:27,352 --> 01:48:40,319
[SPEAKER_02]: Because, again, whatever arises in your experience, has a degree, has an element of solidity in it, has an element of worth present, a phenomenon of worth present.

1372
01:48:41,239 --> 01:48:44,161
[SPEAKER_02]: If you establish upon that, you surmount everything that has that.

1373
01:48:44,441 --> 01:48:50,964
[SPEAKER_02]: And everything has that, which means you surmount everything.

1374
01:48:51,044 --> 01:48:54,806
[SPEAKER_00]: In my case, in my meditation, the practice of what I'm doing,

1375
01:48:56,467 --> 01:48:59,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Those things are actually a bit different things.

1376
01:48:59,908 --> 01:49:13,992
[SPEAKER_02]: In my case... Well, in your case, when you have thoughts coming up, or bubbles, as you refer to it, whatever, it's different perceptions, try not to forget about the general situation you're in.

1377
01:49:15,412 --> 01:49:21,634
[SPEAKER_02]: The fact that you're sitting in your room, on the floor, or on the chair, that's already the situation.

1378
01:49:21,874 --> 01:49:24,215
[SPEAKER_02]: Seated in such and such situation.

1379
01:49:25,313 --> 01:49:26,354
[SPEAKER_02]: That's a general thought.

1380
01:49:26,634 --> 01:49:27,694
[SPEAKER_02]: That's one experience.

1381
01:49:30,016 --> 01:49:40,882
[SPEAKER_02]: Within that, and while you are in that position and that thought, whatever you're thinking of, whatever you're feeling, whatever you're hearing, whatever you're seeing, you can be mindful of that from that perspective.

1382
01:49:41,702 --> 01:49:49,167
[SPEAKER_02]: But if you forget about the general situation, then you'll end up chasing every particular thought or perception at all.

1383
01:49:49,407 --> 01:49:51,588
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's the problem, that there is no mindfulness there.

1384
01:49:53,421 --> 01:49:56,364
[SPEAKER_02]: Or rather, very little mindfulness, not established.

1385
01:50:08,545 --> 01:50:18,558
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I'm not thinking that the need to see all the bubbles is not mine, and that these bubbles are calling it as I am, and self-view, and the dependent relation I have to keep.

1386
01:50:18,578 --> 01:50:26,148
[SPEAKER_02]: No, well, see, the problem with that is, I am seeing all of this, which means your general sense of I remains unaffected.

1387
01:50:28,433 --> 01:50:29,514
[SPEAKER_02]: You have to reverse that.

1388
01:50:29,554 --> 01:50:34,176
[SPEAKER_02]: You have to start indirectly whereby you see yourself first in this situation.

1389
01:50:34,296 --> 01:50:39,278
[SPEAKER_02]: While you're in that situation, whatever is in front of you, you start being mindful of that.

1390
01:50:40,539 --> 01:50:44,200
[SPEAKER_02]: When that mindfulness is established enough, it becomes apparent then.

1391
01:50:45,081 --> 01:50:46,261
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, you don't see it.

1392
01:50:46,341 --> 01:50:47,342
[SPEAKER_02]: You don't invent it.

1393
01:50:47,942 --> 01:50:50,063
[SPEAKER_02]: You just discern it as already there.

1394
01:50:52,824 --> 01:50:54,105
[SPEAKER_02]: And what is already there is that

1395
01:50:55,523 --> 01:51:02,029
[SPEAKER_02]: As I said before, the general situation you're in defines these particular bubbles and thoughts and perceptions.

1396
01:51:02,770 --> 01:51:07,053
[SPEAKER_02]: But they're the ones enabling the general situation to be such in the first place.

1397
01:51:09,155 --> 01:51:09,916
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

1398
01:51:10,256 --> 01:51:16,622
[SPEAKER_02]: So you recognize that the relationship or the dependence between this general and particular level are there.

1399
01:51:17,543 --> 01:51:19,945
[SPEAKER_02]: Not me and I am doing it.

1400
01:51:20,085 --> 01:51:21,066
[SPEAKER_02]: Not in front of me.

1401
01:51:21,166 --> 01:51:21,847
[SPEAKER_02]: Not for me.

1402
01:51:22,743 --> 01:51:23,363
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just there.

1403
01:51:23,984 --> 01:51:25,345
[SPEAKER_02]: Because you're there, sitting in the room.

1404
01:51:25,665 --> 01:51:28,567
[SPEAKER_02]: While you're there, sitting in the room, you're thinking certain things.

1405
01:51:29,687 --> 01:51:33,570
[SPEAKER_02]: While you're there, sitting in the room, on your chair, looking through the window, you're thinking certain things.

1406
01:51:36,491 --> 01:51:41,074
[SPEAKER_02]: Would you be thinking those things, if you're not in that room, sitting on that chair, looking through the window?

1407
01:51:41,735 --> 01:51:43,116
[SPEAKER_02]: You might well not be thinking that.

1408
01:51:44,156 --> 01:51:51,721
[SPEAKER_02]: So, your general situation determines, defines these certain things, defines significance of those things, thought, in that situation.

1409
01:51:53,682 --> 01:52:09,508
[SPEAKER_02]: But then again, if you were not thinking in your room, on your chair, like if there was no chair, there's no room, no window, you're not thinking, would you be able to have a situation of me sitting on the chair, looking through the window, thinking these things?

1410
01:52:10,268 --> 01:52:13,210
[SPEAKER_02]: You couldn't.

1411
01:52:14,230 --> 01:52:17,331
[SPEAKER_02]: So that's how they depend on each other.

1412
01:52:17,371 --> 01:52:19,512
[SPEAKER_02]: And none of it can be yours for that very reason.

1413
01:52:22,353 --> 01:52:26,196
[SPEAKER_00]: The mindfulness of body means not only the body, the situation... Yeah, yeah.

1414
01:52:26,216 --> 01:52:30,499
[SPEAKER_02]: Mindfulness of the body means mindfulness of the situation the body is in.

1415
01:52:30,620 --> 01:52:38,125
[SPEAKER_02]: Not the actual physical posture and observing of like, oh, this is how my knee feels in this pose or something.

1416
01:52:38,145 --> 01:52:42,869
[SPEAKER_02]: That's, that's all already, because you're in that situation, you can look at those particular things.

1417
01:52:44,510 --> 01:52:45,591
[SPEAKER_02]: And you can, if you want.

1418
01:52:46,091 --> 01:52:49,634
[SPEAKER_02]: While you're seated on the floor in a certain posture,

1419
01:52:51,478 --> 01:52:58,725
[SPEAKER_02]: If you start looking particular aspects of your body, your hands, your knees, your feet, your head, again, you can do it rightly, you can do it wrongly.

1420
01:52:59,305 --> 01:53:14,279
[SPEAKER_02]: If you do it rightly, you'll see those particular components being defined by the fact that the body is generally already there, but at the same time, without those particular components, that body couldn't have not arisen as such in the first place.

1421
01:53:16,541 --> 01:53:17,522
[SPEAKER_02]: It's the same principle.

1422
01:53:21,337 --> 01:53:25,702
[SPEAKER_02]: But if you just go at the components, forget about the whole picture, and just say, oh, this is not mine, this is not mine.

1423
01:53:26,943 --> 01:53:30,787
[SPEAKER_02]: Nothing's changed, really.

1424
01:53:33,610 --> 01:53:34,331
[SPEAKER_00]: People say...

1425
01:53:37,240 --> 01:53:43,542
[SPEAKER_00]: If I was thinking this body, that fear, fear, fear, fear this body, and what is this body doing?

1426
01:53:43,902 --> 01:53:45,442
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not that important thing.

1427
01:53:45,462 --> 01:53:50,523
[SPEAKER_00]: Just I only have to keep seeing the feelings arise as a thought, as a bubble in the mind.

1428
01:53:51,003 --> 01:53:55,224
[SPEAKER_00]: And just need to keep knowing that everything's arising, appearing on their own.

1429
01:53:55,424 --> 01:53:57,205
[SPEAKER_00]: So, situation whatsoever.

1430
01:53:57,785 --> 01:53:59,965
[SPEAKER_00]: And you have feelings arising wherever I am.

1431
01:54:00,606 --> 01:54:00,826
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

1432
01:54:00,966 --> 01:54:02,926
[SPEAKER_02]: Again, you can, you can do that.

1433
01:54:03,006 --> 01:54:06,567
[SPEAKER_02]: But even then, you need a reference point in regard to what you're looking at.

1434
01:54:08,744 --> 01:54:11,466
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you might not want to be mindful of the body, that's fine.

1435
01:54:11,526 --> 01:54:14,588
[SPEAKER_02]: If you want to be mindful of the feelings, you need a reference point in regard to that.

1436
01:54:14,968 --> 01:54:19,651
[SPEAKER_02]: In other words, there is always a situation that you have to be mindful of.

1437
01:54:20,492 --> 01:54:22,553
[SPEAKER_02]: There is always more general and more particular.

1438
01:54:23,174 --> 01:54:25,396
[SPEAKER_02]: That's needed for mindfulness to be established.

1439
01:54:25,696 --> 01:54:29,939
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't just be staring at the particular and being mindful, I am mindful.

1440
01:54:31,280 --> 01:54:33,902
[SPEAKER_02]: Or rather, that mindfulness is not really established mindfulness.

1441
01:54:35,503 --> 01:54:35,883
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know.

1442
01:54:40,447 --> 01:54:52,414
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you're mindful of your feelings arising, again, you can be anchored, established in your situation, in terms of bodily posture.

1443
01:54:54,495 --> 01:54:56,636
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm walking, fear arose.

1444
01:54:57,557 --> 01:54:59,338
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm walking, fear is present.

1445
01:55:00,419 --> 01:55:02,360
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm walking, fear is present.

1446
01:55:02,840 --> 01:55:05,401
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm walking, walking, fear is ceasing.

1447
01:55:06,262 --> 01:55:08,003
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm walking, ah, fear is gone.

1448
01:55:09,897 --> 01:55:10,918
[SPEAKER_02]: As opposed to, I'm afraid.

1449
01:55:12,839 --> 01:55:20,483
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, I'm not afraid.

1450
01:55:20,923 --> 01:55:27,527
[SPEAKER_02]: Or, it's slightly more subtle, you can get established in terms of mind object, thought, dhamma.

1451
01:55:28,447 --> 01:55:36,792
[SPEAKER_02]: That's another satipaṭṭhāna, whereby I'm feeling this on account of this memory, or on account of

1452
01:55:38,157 --> 01:55:41,018
[SPEAKER_02]: What somebody said, or kind of something I've seen.

1453
01:55:43,720 --> 01:55:45,121
[SPEAKER_02]: For as long as that reason...

1454
01:55:46,862 --> 01:55:49,483
[SPEAKER_02]: I've seen something unpleasant, I feel bad.

1455
01:55:50,643 --> 01:55:54,185
[SPEAKER_02]: For as long as this unpleasant thing is present, bad feeling endures.

1456
01:55:55,766 --> 01:55:59,528
[SPEAKER_02]: Unpleasant feeling... unpleasant thing ceases, bad feeling is gone.

1457
01:56:01,389 --> 01:56:06,632
[SPEAKER_00]: So, so...

1458
01:56:07,941 --> 01:56:09,583
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in my case, suppose if I...

1459
01:56:11,004 --> 01:56:17,890
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you see the feeling coming from that thing, not from you, belonging to that thing, not to you.

1460
01:56:17,910 --> 01:56:23,995
[SPEAKER_02]: And again, you can see the fear belonging to the body in the situation, not to me, I am afraid.

1461
01:56:24,716 --> 01:56:25,657
[SPEAKER_02]: Because of situation.

1462
01:56:25,717 --> 01:56:26,037
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

1463
01:56:27,218 --> 01:56:33,884
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's how you abandon both, situation and the particular thing that has arisen.

1464
01:56:34,184 --> 01:56:35,225
[SPEAKER_00]: Not because of me.

1465
01:56:35,909 --> 01:56:36,069
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

1466
01:56:36,309 --> 01:56:40,190
[SPEAKER_02]: Because if it's... if it comes from me, me will never be abandoned.

1467
01:56:43,391 --> 01:56:45,892
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's important to see that relation.

1468
01:56:45,912 --> 01:56:51,193
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it not enough, suppose, if I totally forget about the situation when this body is in?

1469
01:56:51,213 --> 01:56:52,233
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't forget about.

1470
01:56:52,533 --> 01:56:53,334
[SPEAKER_02]: You can ignore it.

1471
01:56:54,814 --> 01:56:55,654
[SPEAKER_02]: But it's already there.

1472
01:56:56,354 --> 01:57:01,716
[SPEAKER_00]: In the meditation, suppose, if I just keep seeing the bubbles arising in that angled circle.

1473
01:57:05,180 --> 01:57:13,125
[SPEAKER_02]: The only reason particular things can arise is from the perspective of a more general situation that it's already there.

1474
01:57:14,586 --> 01:57:24,573
[SPEAKER_02]: In other words, the movement of arising and ceasing is impossible if there is no static point in regard to it.

1475
01:57:24,593 --> 01:57:26,495
[SPEAKER_02]: That's just the nature of things.

1476
01:57:26,595 --> 01:57:28,396
[SPEAKER_02]: If everything is moving, there's no movement.

1477
01:57:29,380 --> 01:57:36,562
[SPEAKER_02]: But the fact that you discern bubbles coming and going, means there is a point that is still in regard to that.

1478
01:57:37,323 --> 01:57:38,943
[SPEAKER_02]: And that point is your situation.

1479
01:57:39,203 --> 01:57:42,164
[SPEAKER_02]: It is more general than those particular changing bubbles.

1480
01:57:43,805 --> 01:57:46,166
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you cannot but not have it.

1481
01:57:46,586 --> 01:57:47,566
[SPEAKER_02]: You can only ignore it.

1482
01:57:48,926 --> 01:57:49,627
[SPEAKER_02]: And that's not good.

1483
01:57:53,808 --> 01:57:56,509
[SPEAKER_01]: Does that mean that you can't go to

1484
01:57:57,806 --> 01:58:03,729
[SPEAKER_01]: The Noble Eightfold Path?

1485
01:58:03,789 --> 01:58:08,932
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1486
01:58:08,952 --> 01:58:09,452
[SPEAKER_02]: The whole thing...

1487
01:58:09,572 --> 01:58:14,355
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not... Like, the Eightfold Path are the eight components that need to be developed.

1488
01:58:14,895 --> 01:58:18,557
[SPEAKER_02]: But it's not one, and then you develop two, and then you develop...

1489
01:58:18,617 --> 01:58:24,560
[SPEAKER_02]: In Samādhiti Sutta, the sutta that talks about it, the main sutta, Madhyamika Nine, he says that

1490
01:58:26,180 --> 01:58:31,124
[SPEAKER_02]: Every of those factors is governed by the first factor of the right view.

1491
01:58:32,185 --> 01:58:38,971
[SPEAKER_02]: So, knowing things rightly is the first precondition.

1492
01:58:39,372 --> 01:58:50,762
[SPEAKER_02]: Knowing things rightly would make your meditation right, would make your reading the suttas right, would make your actions right, your sīla right, everything will become right if you know that it's right.

1493
01:58:52,192 --> 01:58:53,853
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's how it's done.

1494
01:58:54,073 --> 01:59:04,118
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the thing is, people misunderstand meditation as a separate thing from contemplating the dhamma, but it's not.

1495
01:59:04,278 --> 01:59:09,300
[SPEAKER_02]: One, like, meditation brings contemplation, contemplation brings meditation.

1496
01:59:10,100 --> 01:59:15,323
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if your meditation is not making any difference to your contemplation, it means that's a wrong meditation.

1497
01:59:16,343 --> 01:59:19,565
[SPEAKER_02]: And he said it's like two yolks pulling each other.

1498
01:59:21,102 --> 01:59:24,427
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if one goes forward, what the other one will have, because they're connected.

1499
01:59:25,228 --> 01:59:28,412
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if you're putting forward samatha, vipassana will be there.

1500
01:59:29,324 --> 01:59:33,447
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not like, oh, I'll do samatha here, then I'll go the other way and do a bit of vipassana there.

1501
01:59:33,987 --> 01:59:34,147
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

1502
01:59:34,208 --> 01:59:37,730
[SPEAKER_02]: If you're doing vipassana, your meditation is coming with it.

1503
01:59:37,770 --> 01:59:40,152
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't even conceive being separate.

1504
01:59:40,232 --> 01:59:44,695
[SPEAKER_02]: And if you read the suttas of meditation, like ānāpānasati, it's all this practice of this mindfulness.

1505
01:59:45,316 --> 01:59:49,419
[SPEAKER_02]: In regard to more general, like, while I'm breathing, I will feel this.

1506
01:59:49,579 --> 01:59:51,060
[SPEAKER_02]: While I'm breathing, I'll think that.

1507
01:59:53,715 --> 02:00:00,229
[SPEAKER_02]: So, being skilled in recognizing situation, you're inevitably... you can't even conceive not being in situation.

1508
02:00:00,730 --> 02:00:03,917
[SPEAKER_02]: Because if you think I'm not in a situation, that is your situation.

1509
02:00:07,083 --> 02:00:18,185
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, you don't even have to constantly think about your situation, but in your daily life, the fact that there are particular things like, oh, I need to sweep this floor now and clean this up.

1510
02:00:18,685 --> 02:00:25,406
[SPEAKER_02]: That's only possible because the floor and the cave and all the significance of the whole thing is already present in my situation.

1511
02:00:26,186 --> 02:00:28,207
[SPEAKER_02]: And then I can attend to these particular things.

1512
02:00:28,667 --> 02:00:30,667
[SPEAKER_00]: I can't forget the situation?

1513
02:00:30,687 --> 02:00:31,387
[SPEAKER_00]: What does it mean?

1514
02:00:31,487 --> 02:00:33,728
[SPEAKER_02]: No, you can forget it, but you can't escape it.

1515
02:00:34,668 --> 02:00:35,828
[SPEAKER_02]: You forget it when you're not mindful.

1516
02:00:38,396 --> 02:00:38,896
[SPEAKER_02]: You ignore it.

1517
02:00:38,916 --> 02:00:40,838
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, you get caught up in particular things.

1518
02:00:41,878 --> 02:00:47,883
[SPEAKER_02]: And then, you suffer more on account of particular things, or you get elated more on account of particular things.

1519
02:00:49,264 --> 02:00:52,786
[SPEAKER_02]: In either way, you get moved much more by the particular things.

1520
02:00:52,866 --> 02:00:53,307
[SPEAKER_02]: You suffer.

1521
02:01:02,834 --> 02:01:04,675
[SPEAKER_02]: That's probably, I don't know, very new for you.

1522
02:01:05,180 --> 02:01:06,360
[SPEAKER_02]: To hear this.

1523
02:01:06,800 --> 02:01:14,622
[SPEAKER_02]: So, but even if it's not, it's not something... it's not something you can just hear somebody say once, and then you... oh, you can get the idea.

1524
02:01:15,183 --> 02:01:16,403
[SPEAKER_02]: But you have to keep doing it.

1525
02:01:17,063 --> 02:01:19,624
[SPEAKER_02]: And, like, the nature of intention works the same.

1526
02:01:20,524 --> 02:01:28,566
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, because you had intention to come here today to see me and talk about the dhamma, that's a very general intention you had.

1527
02:01:30,066 --> 02:01:32,047
[SPEAKER_02]: While that intention was still present,

1528
02:01:33,055 --> 02:01:34,416
[SPEAKER_02]: You went and hired a tuk-tuk.

1529
02:01:35,136 --> 02:01:36,736
[SPEAKER_02]: There was a more particular intention.

1530
02:01:37,037 --> 02:01:40,978
[SPEAKER_02]: Calling the driver, telling him to come, giving him the time.

1531
02:01:42,539 --> 02:01:52,003
[SPEAKER_02]: Walking to the tuk-tuk, sitting in the tuk-tuk, being in the tuk-tuk, coming here, walking, finding the place, getting lost, realizing that you were lost, finding the right way.

1532
02:01:52,123 --> 02:01:58,425
[SPEAKER_02]: All of those particular intentions were within the intention of you wanting to be here, toṭa dhamma.

1533
02:01:59,186 --> 02:02:02,687
[SPEAKER_02]: If that general intention, you wanting to be here, toṭa dhamma, disappears,

1534
02:02:03,835 --> 02:02:07,356
[SPEAKER_02]: But, if you suddenly change your mind on the way here.

1535
02:02:07,536 --> 02:02:09,757
[SPEAKER_02]: Oh, I can't go there today.

1536
02:02:09,777 --> 02:02:10,197
[SPEAKER_02]: That's it.

1537
02:02:10,957 --> 02:02:12,097
[SPEAKER_02]: You go back.

1538
02:02:12,117 --> 02:02:18,279
[SPEAKER_02]: All of those particular intentions, then, lose their general, like a, significant direction.

1539
02:02:20,680 --> 02:02:21,600
[SPEAKER_02]: You change your mind.

1540
02:02:22,000 --> 02:02:25,141
[SPEAKER_02]: Suddenly I called and said I had to go to hospital or something like that.

1541
02:02:25,901 --> 02:02:28,502
[SPEAKER_02]: If the general intention of you wanting to be here

1542
02:02:29,856 --> 02:02:39,682
[SPEAKER_02]: Changes, whether through you or through the circumstances, all of the particular intention, then, oh, I cannot go to there, therefore, why would you be calling a tuk-tuk, telling him to bring you here?

1543
02:02:40,023 --> 02:02:40,763
[SPEAKER_02]: No, that's gone.

1544
02:02:43,145 --> 02:02:50,009
[SPEAKER_02]: If you're about to make a phone call to call a driver, but then you found out that you can't come, you're not going to be doing this particular.

1545
02:02:51,020 --> 02:02:57,283
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's how you can be mindful of all of those particular intentions, by knowing what the general intention is in regard to them.

1546
02:02:57,703 --> 02:03:03,825
[SPEAKER_02]: And, obviously, there is no end to generality, nor there is an end to particularity.

1547
02:03:05,026 --> 02:03:07,267
[SPEAKER_02]: But that's not important.

1548
02:03:08,027 --> 02:03:11,849
[SPEAKER_02]: You won't have to reach the end or the first point, because there won't be any.

1549
02:03:12,629 --> 02:03:14,690
[SPEAKER_02]: The whole point is to understand that relationship.

1550
02:03:16,032 --> 02:03:29,762
[SPEAKER_02]: So, if sometimes you... like, you had an intention to come here, but then your mindfulness is not established upon that intention, well, then you can establish your mindfulness upon even more general intention of... intention of you wanting to understand the dhamma.

1551
02:03:31,284 --> 02:03:36,307
[SPEAKER_02]: As a result of you wanting to understand the dhamma, you want to come here particularly and talk about the dhamma.

1552
02:03:36,928 --> 02:03:44,634
[SPEAKER_02]: As a result of you wanting to understand the dhamma, you want to come here and talk the dhamma, you want to call the tuk-tuk driver and tell him to come at certain time and bring you here.

1553
02:03:45,378 --> 02:03:48,521
[SPEAKER_02]: As a result of all of that, you will sit in a tuk-tuk for two and a half hours.

1554
02:03:49,002 --> 02:03:51,825
[SPEAKER_02]: As a result of all of that, you will be... and so on and so forth.

1555
02:03:53,987 --> 02:03:58,312
[SPEAKER_02]: So you can pick any of those things, as long as you're mindful in regard to the particular.

1556
02:03:58,872 --> 02:04:01,555
[SPEAKER_02]: Not just chase the particular or get lost in the general.

1557
02:04:02,796 --> 02:04:04,198
[SPEAKER_02]: It's the relationship that's important.

1558
02:04:04,959 --> 02:04:08,042
[SPEAKER_02]: And that relationship is sankhāra-sankhāta-dhamma.

1559
02:04:09,118 --> 02:04:11,300
[SPEAKER_02]: The whole experience is dual in that sense.

1560
02:04:11,360 --> 02:04:13,141
[SPEAKER_02]: Everything, every experience falls into that.

1561
02:04:13,462 --> 02:04:16,524
[SPEAKER_02]: That's the... That's when you're calling it fundamental structure.

1562
02:04:16,924 --> 02:04:19,346
[SPEAKER_02]: It's the structure of the experience, the structure of the aggregates.

1563
02:04:20,627 --> 02:04:31,056
[SPEAKER_02]: And the Buddha said, even if somebody is remembering one previous life, five previous lives, five hundred previous lives, all they're remembering is these five or one among them.

1564
02:04:31,757 --> 02:04:33,318
[SPEAKER_02]: These five aggregates or one among them.

1565
02:04:33,998 --> 02:04:35,219
[SPEAKER_02]: Nothing, nothing out of that.

1566
02:04:36,040 --> 02:04:36,581
[SPEAKER_02]: It's all within

1567
02:04:37,735 --> 02:04:41,217
[SPEAKER_02]: It's all within the same structure.

1568
02:04:41,378 --> 02:04:49,263
[SPEAKER_00]: Intention and this choosing, these things are actually really confusing, because, like, the sense of self is really, like, intended.

1569
02:04:49,283 --> 02:04:53,886
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, it's the most, it's the closest, closest relation.

1570
02:04:54,467 --> 02:04:56,948
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, intention is there, where the sense of self is.

1571
02:04:56,988 --> 02:05:05,995
[SPEAKER_02]: But again, if you start looking in terms of the situation, the only reason you can intend to drink that glass of water is because it's already there in your situation.

1572
02:05:07,067 --> 02:05:10,529
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the particular intention... Well, exactly.

1573
02:05:10,549 --> 02:05:12,990
[SPEAKER_02]: You can choose what's already given.

1574
02:05:14,191 --> 02:05:19,894
[SPEAKER_02]: If it hasn't been given and displayed through your senses, you can't even conceive it, let alone intend it.

1575
02:05:22,355 --> 02:05:31,020
[SPEAKER_02]: But if you're just looking and focusing on the particular, then your intention will always feel very direct, always feel me and I am.

1576
02:05:32,060 --> 02:05:33,821
[SPEAKER_02]: But, yeah, I want to drink water.

1577
02:05:34,162 --> 02:05:36,543
[SPEAKER_02]: But the only reason I can drink water is because there is water here.

1578
02:05:37,431 --> 02:05:45,197
[SPEAKER_02]: Drinkable water, and there's a little... And then you realize, even this whole sense of, I want to do this, is actually determined by that general situation.

1579
02:05:45,838 --> 02:05:53,704
[SPEAKER_02]: Because if that thing changes, no matter how strong my sense of self is, if there is no water to drink it here, that intention will not make sense.

1580
02:05:54,605 --> 02:05:55,746
[SPEAKER_02]: And I might have to go somewhere else.

1581
02:05:57,087 --> 02:05:58,308
[SPEAKER_00]: So it's totally up to you.

1582
02:05:58,548 --> 02:06:04,453
[SPEAKER_02]: No, I think it is... Well, if you start looking through a situation, the relationship becomes more and more apparent.

1583
02:06:05,586 --> 02:06:12,150
[SPEAKER_02]: The relationship that is mutually determining and kind of not requiring your sense of self at all.

1584
02:06:14,971 --> 02:06:20,054
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the more you are aware of it, the more you discern it, the less of it is yours.

1585
02:06:20,094 --> 02:06:26,097
[SPEAKER_02]: Externally, not much can change, not much needs to change.

1586
02:06:26,177 --> 02:06:29,379
[SPEAKER_02]: Obviously, virtues, behavior and so on, but that's it.

1587
02:06:31,340 --> 02:06:34,262
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it is actually quite important that it all arises.

1588
02:06:35,039 --> 02:06:35,570
[SPEAKER_00]: What kind of...

